# 5. Minimum production launch checklist

## Customer

- [ ] Customer can discover only appropriately labelled vendors.
- [ ] Unclaimed vendors cannot accept orders.
- [ ] Menu items and prices come from the server.
- [ ] Cart supports quantity, options, and separate vendors.
- [ ] Confirmation is explicit and immutable.
- [ ] Customer receives a receipt and tracking link.
- [ ] Customer can cancel according to state.
- [ ] Customer receives safe substitution choices.
- [ ] Arabic, English, Arabizi, and French behavior is tested.

## Merchant

- [ ] Merchant identity and membership are verified.
- [ ] Merchant has a primary and backup notification path.
- [ ] Merchant portal works on tablet/mobile browser.
- [ ] WhatsApp card and template fallback are tested.
- [ ] Accept/reject actions are authenticated and idempotent.
- [ ] Merchant can pause and resume orders.
- [ ] Merchant can mark items unavailable.
- [ ] Merchant can set preparation time and ready state.
- [ ] Merchant timeout creates an operations task.

## Driver

- [ ] Driver identity and vehicle requirements are reviewed.
- [ ] Driver belongs to an active zone.
- [ ] Driver sees only assigned delivery information.
- [ ] Driver receives exact COD amount when relevant.
- [ ] Driver location becomes stale safely.
- [ ] Customer address and landmark are clear.
- [ ] Pickup and delivery proof are recorded.
- [ ] Not-collected and failed-delivery workflows are tested.

## Payments

- [ ] COD limits are enforced.
- [ ] Payment provider is approved and documented.
- [ ] Payment amount and currency are verified server-side.
- [ ] Webhooks are signed and idempotent.
- [ ] Refunds are recorded in the ledger.
- [ ] Settlement reconciliation exists.
- [ ] No card data is stored by Alo King.
- [ ] Provider and legal questions are answered in writing.

## Security and privacy

- [ ] RLS is tested by role.
- [ ] Service-role access is restricted.
- [ ] Secrets are outside Git.
- [ ] Logs are redacted.
- [ ] Tracking tokens expire.
- [ ] Customer deletion commands bypass the model.
- [ ] Marketing opt-in and opt-out are separate from service consent.
- [ ] Data retention and vendor/provider access are documented.

## Operations

- [ ] Support inbox exists.
- [ ] Every order has an operations timeline.
- [ ] Failed notifications are visible.
- [ ] Human escalation is defined.
- [ ] Zone pause and merchant pause are tested.
- [ ] Daily reconciliation is assigned to a person.
- [ ] Incident runbook exists.
- [ ] Rollback plan exists.

